cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "vaultlab: An open-source AI laboratory for biological researchers"
message: "If you use vaultlab, please cite both the software and the preprint."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ni"
    given-names: "Bobby Y.X."
    affiliation: "Hickey Lab, Duke University Biomedical Engineering"
version: "0.0.1"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bobbyni819/vaultlab"
url: "https://github.com/bobbyni819/vaultlab"
abstract: >
  vaultlab is an open-source software framework that integrates literature
  search, citation verification, wet-lab data analysis, publication-quality
  figure generation, manuscript drafting, and slide deck creation in a single
  repository designed for use with the Claude Code agentic IDE. vaultlab
  wraps established Python libraries (scanpy, squidpy, scikit-image, Cellpose)
  for canonical bioinformatics analyses and adds a Claude-driven orchestration
  layer that surfaces literature, verifies citations against source passages
  with semantic matching, and produces NotebookLM-style evidence-on-demand
  for manuscript drafts.
keywords:
  - "AI lab"
  - "scientific computing"
  - "spatial omics"
  - "single-cell RNA-seq"
  - "manuscript drafting"
  - "citation verification"
  - "Claude Code"
  - "Obsidian"
  - "knowledge base"
  - "research companion"
